      "id": 330136,
      "name": "Season 12",
      "overview": "Connected or Connected and Connected + is an Israeli daily docu-reality series, in which several participants, men in the \"Connected\" season or women in the \"Connected\" season, or women and men together from the fifth season when the show was called \"Connected +\", document themselves. In each season, the show follows 5 or 6 participants who document their lives independently, without the involvement of camera crews. Each participant receives a video camera and is instructed on how to document and mediate their daily routine. Over time, the participants in the show become photographers and directors who use the camera to draw their own story. The thousands of hours of raw material are edited by the series' director and creators into 35 22-minute episodes. The show's format has been sold to a production company and broadcasting channels in about 17 countries, including Denmark, France, Ireland, India, Norway and Finland.",
